.TH CASEMATE 1 "" "casemate" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
casemate \- password-based file encryption (AES-256-GCM, Argon2id)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B casemate
.I command
.RI [ flags ]
.RI [ file... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B casemate
encrypts and decrypts files with a password, optionally combined with a key file.
Directories are packed into a tar archive first.
Data goes to standard output; prompts, progress and errors go to standard error.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B encrypt
Encrypt files, writing
.IR file .enc,
or directories, writing
.IR dir .tar.enc.
.TP
.B decrypt
Decrypt files, stripping
.BR .enc .
With
.BR \-extract ,
unpack a directory archive into a new directory.
.TP
.B rekey
Re-encrypt files in place with the current format, optionally with a new password or key file.
With
.B \-recursive
a directory argument is searched for encrypted files;
.B \-dry\-run
lists what would be rekeyed without writing.
.TP
.B info
Show a file's format without decrypting it. With
.B \-json
print one JSON object per file.
.TP
.B keygen
Create a random key file with
.BR "\-out " \fIpath\fR.
.TP
.B version
Show version information.
.SH COMMON FLAGS
.TP
.BI \-file " path"
Input file, repeatable; \- reads standard input.
.TP
.BI \-out " path"
Output file (single input only); \- writes standard output.
.TP
.BI \-password\-file " path"
Read the password from the first line of a file.
.TP
.BI \-password\-env " name"
Read the password from an environment variable.
.TP
.BI \-password\-fd " n"
Read the password from a file descriptor (3 or higher).
.TP
.BI \-keyfile " path"
Use a key file as a second factor.
.TP
.B \-strict
Refuse a password file others can read and a new password under 12 characters.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 if an operation failed, 2 for invalid flags.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
casemate encrypt notes.txt
casemate decrypt notes.txt.enc
tar -czf \- project | casemate encrypt \-file \- \-out project.tgz.enc
casemate rekey \-recursive \-dry\-run ~/vault
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/dterana/casemate
